===Etymology===
Attested from {{circa2|1600}}. Compare {{cog|nl|hè|t=huh}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hʌ/|[hʌ̃]|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-huh.wav|a=Southern England|q=rising pitch}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-huh2.wav|a=Southern England|q=falling pitch}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-huh3.wav|a=Southern England|q=martial arts}}
* {{IPA|en|/hʌ/|[hʌ̃]|/hə/|[hə̃]|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-huh.ogg|a=California}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌ|s=1}}

===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# {{sid|en|confusion}} {{lb|en|with rising pitch}} {{ng|Used to express [[doubt]] or [[confusion]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Huh?''' Where did they go?}}
# {{lb|en|with falling pitch}} {{ng|Used to express [[amusement]] or subtle [[surprise]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Huh!''' I'm sure I locked it when I left.}}
# {{lb|en|with rising pitch}} {{ng|Used to [[reinforce]] a [[question]].}}
#: {{ux|en|Where were you last night? '''Huh'''?}}
# {{lb|en|slang|with falling pitch}} {{ng|Used either to [[belittle]] the issuer of a statement/question, or [[sarcasm|sarcastically]] to indicate utter agreement, and that the statement being responded to is an extreme [[understatement]]. The intonation is changed to distinguish between the two meanings - implied [[dullness]] for belittlement, and [[feigned]] [[surprise]] for utter agreement.}}
#: {{ux|en|(belittlement) A: "We should go to an amusement park; it would be fun." B: "'''Huh.'''"}}
#: {{ux|en|(agreement) A: "Murder is bad." B: "'''Huh!'''"}}
# {{lb|en|informal|with rising pitch}} {{non-gloss|Used to indicate that one did not hear what was said.}}
#: {{syn|en|come again|pardon|what|Thesaurus:say again}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Huh'''? Could you speak up?}}
# {{lb|en|informal|with falling pitch}} {{non-gloss|Used to create a [[tag question]].}}
#: {{ux|en|It's getting kind of late, '''huh?'''}}
# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} {{ng|Representing the sound of heavy [[breathing#Noun|breathing]].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Donald McCaig|title=The Butte Polka: A Novel|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Rawson, Wade Publishers, Inc.|year=1980|page=251|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/buttepolkanovel00mcca/page/251/mode/1up|isbn=0-892-56133-5|passage=He broke into a dogtrot and ran by us. I don't think he saw us. His voice was coming in little puffs, '''huh''', '''huh''', '''huh''', but he probably didn't notice that either.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Robert Purchese|quotee=w:Marcin Iwiński|title=Seeing Red: The story of CD Projekt|work=w:Eurogamer|url=https://www.eurogamer.net/seeing-red-the-story-of-cd-projekt|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260925092534/https://www.eurogamer.net/seeing-red-the-story-of-cd-projekt|archivedate=25 September 2026|date=15 May 2019|passage=It was up so many flights of stairs that people would arrive for meetings drenched in sweat: "They were like '''huh''' '''huh''' '''huh''' [panting] - where the hell are you?!"}}
# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} {{n-g|Representing a [[chuckling#Noun|chuckling]] sound.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=Katherine Knorr|title=Lambert Wilson: A Man of New Faith|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2010/12/07/arts/07iht-wilson.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250823233904/https://www.nytimes.com/2010/12/07/arts/07iht-wilson.html|archivedate=23 August 2025|date=7 December 2010|passage=Mr. [[w:Lambert Wilson|&#91;Lambert&#93; Wilson]] says this with a soft chuckle, sounding a bit like '''huh''' '''huh''' '''huh'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Meg Howrey|title=The Wanderers|location=London{{nb...}}|publisher=[[w:Charles Scribner's Sons|Scribner]]|year=2017|page=173|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/wanderers0000howr_v5z7/page/n10/mode/1up|isbn=1-471-14666-9|passage=Helen starts laughing, properly now. '''''Huh'''''-'''''huh'''''-'''''huh'''''.}}
# {{lb|en|martial arts}} {{n-g|A [[kiai#Noun|kiai]], shouted as a limb is swung in attack.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ashaki Boelter|title=The Nok|location=Bend, O.R.|publisher=Shakalot High Entertainment<!--self-published-->|year=1993|year_published=2006|page=69|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/nok0000boel/page/69/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-972-10676-4|passage=Shawn quickly turns around and punches the pale hand, yelling "'''Huh'''! '''Huh'''! Hi yah'! '''Huh'''! Get off me! Yeah!"}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Neal Pollack|quotee=David Nelson|title=King of the Creature Feature|work=w:Chicago Reader|url=https://chicagoreader.com/news-politics/king-of-the-creature-feature/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231101094542/https://chicagoreader.com/news-politics/king-of-the-creature-feature/|archivedate=1 November 2023|location=Chicago, I.L.|publisher=Chicago Reader, Inc.|date=5 October 1995|issn=1096-6919|oclc=1105307753|passage=He gets out of the chair, whips off his jacket, and starts closing in on the camera, punching rapidly as he moves. A left hook, a right jab. "Hey, I'm a boxer and a marine! So don't mess with me, man! Semper fi! Marine Corps! They better not mess with me! My critics better not mess with me, man, 'cause I'm gonna beat you up. '''Huh''', '''huh''', '''huh''', '''huh''', '''huh'''. Hmm, hmmm, hmm, hmmmm, heeeyah, '''huh''', '''huh'''. Hmmm, yeah!"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Larry Swartz|title=Dramathemes: Classroom Literacy that Will Excite, Surprise, and Stimulate Learning|location=Markham, Ont.|publisher=Pembroke Publishers Limited|year=2014|page=130-131|pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=pZjVBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA130|isbn=978-1-551-38300-2|passage=Student A has both arms outstretched in a karate motion and shouts out "'''HUH'''". Student B receives the sound by putting both arms straight in the air and yelling "'''HUH'''". Students on either side of ''B'' give ''B'' a karate chop by miming a sideways karate chop — without any touching.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Dwayne Reed|title=Simon B. Rhymin' Gets in the Game|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Little, Brown Books for Young Readers|year=2023|page=unnumbered|pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=5cV_EAAAQBAJ&pg=PT58|isbn=978-0-316-44175-9|passage='''HUH'''-'''HUH''', HI-YAH!}}

